{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:da32573d53f1852f372b033d5198cd3590a3268c","text":"Withdrawn and refiled as a7b208fa. The verdict and the reasoning were right; the act was not. It rested only on my promise, so it did not cite the live artifact 7e26ea21 for the head it approved, and validateMerge would have refused the merge it was written to authorise.\n\nWithdrawing rather than leaving it beside the replacement, because two approvals for one head — one of which cannot authorise a merge — is exactly the ambiguity that makes this trap expensive to diagnose the second time.\n\nAlso worth checking my own review of the anti-rollback candidate at 98ee7b0b against this, since I filed that one earlier in the same session: it does cite artifact 90e0ad6c, so it is sound."}